.policy "ruff-dtz002-call-datetime-today" revision 2
.description "Use datetime.now with a timezone instead of datetime.today; today returns a naive local time with no zone information."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff DTZ002 (flake8-datetimez): `datetime.datetime.today()`, which returns the naive local time. A call
// followed by `.astimezone()` (through any `.replace(…)`) is aware and not reported. Reported at the call. Only
// in a file that imports datetime.
//   datetime.datetime.today()                    ← DTZ002
//   datetime.datetime.today().astimezone()       not reported
#include "python/datetime.rr"

.violation DTZ002(at: node) code "DTZ002"
    "Replace `today()` with `now(tz=...)`, passing the zone you mean (`datetime.timezone.utc` for UTC) so the result is aware. Keep `today()` only where a naive local time is required."
    suppress ruff "DTZ002"
DTZ002(c) :- dt_call(c, "datetime.datetime.today"), !then_astimezone(c).
